    <!-- Doomscrolling & Digital Wellbeing Awareness -->
    <string name="wellbeing_title">Digital Wellbeing &amp; Fake Dopamine</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_manifesto_badge">NOT A GAME • AWARENESS TOOL</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_manifesto_body">Scroll-Meter NEVER encourages you to scroll more. Its sole mission is to make invisible compulsive screen scrolling physically tangible — so you can put your phone down.</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_fake_dopamine_title">The Slot Machine Dopamine Trap</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_fake_dopamine_desc">Infinite feeds exploit variable reward schedules. Each swipe delivers micro-dopamine bursts that trick the brain into an endless craving cycle without real fulfillment.</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_brain_fog_title">Cognitive Fragmentation &amp; Brain Fog</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_brain_fog_desc">Rapid content switching degrades deep focus, shortens attention span, and exhausts executive brain function.</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_thumb_strain_title">Physical Deformity &amp; Smartphone Thumb</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_thumb_strain_desc">Repetitive micro-swipes cause De Quervain tenosynovitis (thumb tendonitis) and cervical spine pressure (Text Neck).</string>
    <string name="wellbeing_tip_take_break">Pro-tip: Set your phone face-down for 20 minutes when reaching your daily goal.</string>

